(Cells are the basic structural and functional units of all living organisms. The cell) Tj T*
(theory states that all living things are composed of cells, that the cell is the smallest) Tj T*
(unit of life, and that new cells arise only from existing cells. Prokaryotic cells lack a) Tj T*
(membrane-bound nucleus, while eukaryotic cells keep their DNA inside a nucleus. Bacteria) Tj T*
(are prokaryotes, whereas plants, animals and fungi are eukaryotes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The plasma membrane surrounds every cell and controls which substances enter and leave. It) Tj T*
(is built from a phospholipid bilayer in which proteins are embedded. Because the membrane) Tj T*
(lets some molecules cross but not others, it is described as selectively permeable.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
