(Mitochondria are the organelles where cellular respiration produces most of the cell's) Tj T*
(ATP. Cellular respiration breaks down glucose in the presence of oxygen and releases) Tj T*
(carbon dioxide and water. Glycolysis is the first stage of respiration and takes place in) Tj T*
(the cytoplasm. The Krebs cycle occurs in the mitochondrial matrix, and the electron) Tj T*
(transport chain is located on the inner mitochondrial membrane.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One molecule of glucose yields about 30 to 32 molecules of ATP through aerobic) Tj T*
(respiration. Glycolysis alone produces a net gain of 2 ATP per glucose molecule. When) Tj T*
(oxygen is scarce, muscle cells switch to fermentation, which regenerates NAD+ and produces) Tj T*
(lactate.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
