(Chloroplasts are the organelles that carry out photosynthesis in plant and algal cells.) Tj T*
(Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose. Chlorophyll) Tj T*
(is the green pigment that absorbs light, mainly in the blue and red wavelengths. The) Tj T*
(light-dependent reactions occur in the thylakoid membranes and split water, releasing) Tj T*
(oxygen. The Calvin cycle takes place in the stroma and fixes carbon dioxide into sugar.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Ribosomes are the sites of protein synthesis. They read messenger RNA and link amino acids) Tj T*
(together in the order specified by the genetic code. Ribosomes can float freely in the) Tj T*
(cytoplasm or be attached to the rough endoplasmic reticulum, which gives it its studded) Tj T*
(appearance.) Tj T*
ET
