(The cell cycle is the sequence of growth and division that a cell goes through. Interphase) Tj T*
(is the longest phase, during which the cell grows and copies its DNA. Mitosis divides the) Tj T*
(nucleus into two genetically identical nuclei and has four stages: prophase, metaphase,) Tj T*
(anaphase and telophase. Cytokinesis then splits the cytoplasm to form two daughter cells.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Meiosis is a special type of division that produces gametes with half the number of) Tj T*
(chromosomes. A human body cell contains 46 chromosomes, so a human gamete contains 23) Tj T*
(chromosomes. Crossing over during meiosis exchanges genetic material between homologous) Tj T*
(chromosomes and increases variation.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
